docs/architecture.md:221:> **In-app browser profiles.** Each tab picks one persistent Electron partition before its first navigation and keeps it for life, because Electron cannot change an attached guest's partition. Partition names are the identity: `persist:paseo-browser` is Shared › default and keeps the cookies of tabs from before profiles; `persist:paseo-shared-<slug>` is a named shared profile; `persist:paseo-project-<scope>-<slug>` is a project profile, where `<scope>` is 32 hex characters of SHA-256 over `["v1","project",serverId,projectId]`, and the automatic workspace profile uses slug `ws-<32 hex>` over the server, project and workspace IDs. Display names never enter a partition name, so renames keep sign-ins. Main admits only these exact forms at `will-attach-webview`. Named profiles live in the main-owned catalog `<userData>/browser-profiles.json`; the tab's choice and first-navigation phase live in its `workspace-browser-store` record. After every `did-attach`, the renderer registers its browser id, workspace id, partition and current guest `WebContents` id, and main accepts it only when that guest belongs to the calling renderer and its session matches the partition. Registration is intentionally repeated because reparenting a retained `<webview>` can replace its guest without replacing the DOM element. Settings > Browser > Clear browser data clears every on-disk Paseo partition plus the sessions of live guests, and reloads those guests without deleting the catalog or saved tabs.
docs/browser-capture-harness.md:62:The toolbar profile journey runs in the [desktop browser regression](testing.md#desktop-browser-regression).
docs/testing.md:151:Its last step is the per-tab browser profile journey. It relaunches Electron once, so two tabs on one origin keep different accounts and their toolbar labels, then clears all profiles through Settings. Run only that journey with `PASEO_DESKTOP_BROWSER_PROFILES_ONLY=1`. Set `PASEO_DESKTOP_BROWSER_E2E_ARTIFACT_DIR` to keep its screenshots and `profiles.json`.
